# Tailwind CSS Best Practices

## Project Setup
- Prefer existing `@theme` tokens in `src/main.css` over new hex in templates
- Configure theme extension properly
- Use Tailwind v4 Vite plugin already in this repo
- Use semantic color names (`brand`, `surface-*`, `content-*`)
- Implement dark mode via the `.dark` class, not ad-hoc palettes

## Component Styling
- Use utility classes over custom CSS
- Group related utilities with @apply when needed
- Use proper responsive design utilities
- Use proper state variants
- Keep component styles consistent

## Layout
- Use Flexbox and Grid utilities effectively
- Implement proper spacing system
- Implement proper responsive breakpoints
- Use proper padding and margin utilities
- Implement proper alignment utilities

## Typography
- Use proper font size utilities
- Implement proper line height
- Use proper font weight utilities
- Use proper text alignment

## Colors
- Use semantic color naming
- Implement proper color contrast
- Use opacity utilities effectively
- Use proper hover states
- Do not introduce shadcn/ui unless the user asks

## Responsive Design
- Use mobile-first approach
- Implement proper breakpoints
- Handle different screen sizes properly
- Implement proper responsive spacing

## Performance
- Minimize custom CSS
- Optimize for production
